The legal text is the Constitution of the Republic of Tajikistan, an official legislative text, as published
by the Majlisi namoyandagon of the Majlisi Oli (parlament.tj, page "Konstitutsiyai JT", Internet Archive
capture of 7 June 2017) and compared with the copy of the Majlisi milli (majmilli.tj, capture of 7 March 2018).

Laws and other official documents are not protected by copyright in Tajikistan: the Law on Copyright and
Related Rights (13 November 1998, as amended), article 7, excludes official documents of a legislative,
administrative or judicial character from protection.

Changes made by Lexifina: the web page was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing was normalised; the Belarusian letter "ў" was written as the Tajik "ӯ"; and the text was arranged
as a git commit credited to its publisher. The wording of the law was not changed. This text is the edition
with the 1999 and 2003 referendum amendments and does not include the amendments of the referendum of
22 May 2016. The Majlisi namoyandagon does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools)
are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
